	<tr>
		<td align="Center">
								<p class="newsTitle">
									Take a deep breath - 
									8/25/2005 5:34:21 AM
								</p>
								<div class="newsBody">
									Well we did it, Saryrn has been bested 4 times each time a WIN congrats goes out to all you OR raiders and leaders!&nbsp; On Friday Aug. 19 OR had their first win aganist Agnarr....woot way to go Jetta for leading it and to all the raiders that attended, for those that went above and beyond "hats off to you all". <br />Now we have added Rallos Zek the Warlord.......muhahaha Please give us time to get our game plans together before our first encounter. If you have never encountered him, he is the very tough to beat and will need your FULL UNDIVIDED ATTENTION from start to finish. Many guilds fail him many times over before a win so be prepared.<br />Current targets on rotation now are: TZ/VZ (last one coming soon), LMM, Agnarr, RZ
								</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td>
								<div class="newsSeperator">&nbsp;</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td class="grid_col2" align="Center">
								<p class="newsTitle">
									TWO to GO! - 
									8/7/2005 8:11:20 PM
								</p>
								<div class="newsBody">
									Well ORians.......the time is near we have bested Carpin and Bert to the end. Now we have added Agnarr to our Kill List, he too shall be defeated by the strength of OR. Our Kill List now contains the following.....Saryrn, LMM, Agnarr, and Tallon/Vallon Zek. Congrats to all those whom stand by your fellow ORians and show support both on official and nonofficial raids. Your Leads are proud of you all....now we just need to stay focused on these last few PoP Gods and we will reach Elementals together. On a side note once Saryrn cycle is done we will be adding our last PoP God.........Rallos Zek the Warlord.
								</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td>
								<div class="newsSeperator">&nbsp;</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td align="Center">
								<p class="newsTitle">
									Saryrn and her little bird, too! - 
									6/8/2005 6:35:34 AM
								</p>
								<div class="newsBody">
									After many ORians spent long hours helping to get Jetta's Saryrn key, we tackled Saryrn for the first time last night!&nbsp; It was a long raid, but thank goodness not as long as reports indicated.&nbsp; We went through all the mini bosses and took out Keeper of Sorrows on our way up.&nbsp; After struggling through the "getting there" part (which we couldn't have done without help from Darknyss and Irinar), Saryrn was a breeze.&nbsp; Besides getting the flags, we took home six different upgrades so the raid was a great success!<br /><br />Great job by everyone: leads and our raiders!<br /><br />New to OR?&nbsp; Please visit <a href="/forums/threadlist.aspx?fid=7194">this link</a> and read the posts marked "READ ME."<br />
								</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td>
								<div class="newsSeperator">&nbsp;</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td class="grid_col2" align="Center">
								<p class="newsTitle">
									Carprin Cycle - 
									5/14/2005 7:09:34 AM
								</p>
								<div class="newsBody">
									Last night we had our first success versus Carprin Deatharn on our first attempt!&nbsp; The infamous Avhi (the skeleton boss) went over like a charm, no deaths, no skellies spawned.&nbsp; It was over before you could say "Carprin who?"&nbsp; Great job by Sinead leading, and to all our assistant raid leaders (not to mention the raiders: excellent job following instructions)!&nbsp; Looking forward to an equally smooth ride on Tuesday.
								</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td>
								<div class="newsSeperator">&nbsp;</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td align="Center">
								<p class="newsTitle">
									Terris Thule finally falls! - 
									4/12/2005 10:30:21 PM
								</p>
								<div class="newsBody">
									After three frustrating wipes versus Terris Thule and her dream defilers we finally succeeded in vanquishing this leading lady!&nbsp; That&nbsp;finishes a resounding round of victories for us in tier 1 planes: Grummus, MB, and Terris Thule.&nbsp; We're not immediately planning to advance to tier 2, though.&nbsp; We'll have <em>at least</em> one more raid against each of those three nasties before we progress.<br /><br />This was our second night of loot distribution via the dkp system and I'm really happy with how that's going: everyone has been really supportive and loot has been spread out so far.&nbsp; Grats to Repets and Jenx on their shiny new shoulders from last night: our first loot from Terris Thule!<br /><br />Thanks again to Kusin for leading the raid; Busygirl, Sunscape, Arekusu, and Rhazzor for organizing our channels; Jadedone and Kierowyn for being looters; and everyone else who helped lead, organize, and win the raid!
								</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td>
								<div class="newsSeperator">&nbsp;</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td class="grid_col2" align="Center">
								<p class="newsTitle">
									Grummus Falls! - 
									3/18/2005 10:20:42 PM
								</p>
								<div class="newsBody">
									OR's first official raid on Friday March 18th took down Grummus in PoDisease to kick off our major planar progression raids.&nbsp; We had a great turnout: over 72 people joined us to get flags, loot, and help friends.&nbsp; We had a few too many deaths due to Grummus' dots, but there's always room for improvement!&nbsp; Look for our next official raid next Friday, and in the meantime keep an eye out for mini-raids, in particular lately Kusin's raids to PoStorms for BoT keys.
								</div>
							</td>
	</tr>
